{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "meta": {
    "comment": "Phase-3 breakthrough tables (ROADMAP 'Breakthroughs (requirements, results, bottlenecks)'). One entry per realm id — the canonical 15-tier DESIGN.md ladder, in tier order — consumed by the BreakthroughSystem (js/systems/breakthroughs.js): requiredProgress is the cultivation.realmProgress gate — the ONLY gate. Per the confirmed design decision (2026-08-11), breakthroughs no longer gate on spirit stones or on item (bottleneck) requirements. cost.spiritStones and bottleneck are kept as INFORMATIONAL fields for future reuse once item/stone sources exist (P4+); they do NOT block an attempt and are NOT consumed/charged in the current game loop (bottleneck ids reference data/items/items.json only). results is the weighted outcome table. Canonical outcomes: perfect, great-success, success, barely-successful (SUCCESS — advance one tier), failure (progressLoss 0), heavy-failure (progressLoss 0.5), qi-deviation (progressLoss 1). Death is excluded in v1 — DESIGN.md marks it 'future optional'. Per-realm success weight is ~80% and failure ~20% (placeholder balancing — Phase 10 Balancing retunes). requiredProgress is the P0-rebalanced pacing curve (2026-08-15, user-directed): at the 20 qi/s base rate the first breakthrough (9 sub-layers at the Mortal base 125 — the panel's Advance Layer gate lights at the base, so a player clears each layer in ~7s) lands in ~1 minute, rising to hours in the late game under the realm cultivationSpeedMultiplier ladder — guarded by tests/perf/pacing.test.mjs (first breakthrough < 2 min) and the data monotonicity check in tests/data/breakthroughs.test.mjs. cost.spiritStones stays a monotonic placeholder curve (0 for mortal)."
  },
